# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Forms/ - allow-listed, not blanket-tracked.
#
# Exactly three documents belong in this repository:
#   Account_Opening_Form_blank template.pdf  the field schema is derived from this
#                                            file, so the pipeline cannot be rebuilt
#                                            without it - it is not a sample, it is
#                                            a source
#   Cif-form.pdf, cif-2.pdf                  dummy-data samples, scored against the
#                                            ground truth in tests/
#
# Everything else dropped into Forms/ is ignored, because the next PDF to land here
# is a real customer's account opening form - name, CNIC, address, income. Ignoring
# by default means committing customer PII takes a deliberate `git add -f` instead
# of an absent-minded `git add -A`.
#
# Two ways to get this wrong:
#   - a blanket *.pdf rule would exclude the blank template, and the project cannot
#     be rebuilt from a clone without it
#   - tracking all of Forms/ (what this used to do) makes leaking a customer form
#     the default behaviour of `git add -A`
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Forms/*
!Forms/Account_Opening_Form_blank template.pdf
!Forms/Cif-form.pdf
!Forms/cif-2.pdf

# ── Generated pipeline artefacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything under build/ is derived and rebuilt by the pipeline:
#   template_schema.json  <- python src/build_schema.py
#   registered/ fields/ reads/ output/ qa/  <- per-document, regenerated per run
#
# build/uploads/ holds forms uploaded through the web UI. On a real form that is
# customer PII, so this must never reach a repository.
/build/

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# virtual environments
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Node / frontend ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# frontend/.gitignore already covers node_modules, dist and logs; this catches
# the archived bundle, which its `dist` pattern does not match.
frontend/dist.zip
frontend/node_modules/

# ── Editors and OS clutter ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Scratch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.tmp
